The `@todo-sequence` declarations in member `.tip` files are authoritative;
this numbered list is the human-readable projection.

### Stage Gates
- [ ] Finish every phase and required verification in the current stage before
  beginning implementation in the next stage.
- [ ] Within each stage, stabilize migrations/models, repository/service policy,
  handlers/protocols, and adversarial tests before adding user or operator UI.
- [ ] Build UI only from shared Skaia primitives and complete loading, empty,
  denied, stale, error, success, responsive, keyboard, and screen-reader states.
- [ ] Keep provider-specific language and behavior inside optional adapters;
  core routes, entities, permissions, feature flags, and UI labels stay generic
  and tenant-configurable.
- [ ] After every stage, update affected specs and this tip with verification,
  newly discovered dependencies, and the next unblocked stage.

### Next Steps
- [ ] Continue `db_transactions_concurrency` with checkout/provider idempotency,
  transition guards, durable fulfilment records and leases, recovery behavior,
  and PostgreSQL-backed concurrency verification.
- [ ] Do not begin status or product UI merely to demonstrate progress; expose
  UI only after the corresponding authoritative backend contract passes its gate.

